    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A warm Byrne Malone welcome to 17 The Arches, Castle Farm, another turnkey home, that we are delighted to present to the market! This A-rated 2 bedroom mid-terraced property is bound to impress with its immaculately styled interiors, central location and gorgeous garden!\n\nThe floorplan of number 17 comprises 88 sqm approx of generously proportioned rooms with an abundance of clever storage solutions throughout. The style and quality of the home is immediately evident on entering, where you are first greeted by a spacious entrance hall with quality flooring and chic Scandinavian style glass panelled doors maximising the light throughout the space. \n\nTo the left of the hall is the kitchen with contemporary fitted kitchen cabinets complemented by sleek countertops, stainless steel sink and taps along with elegant subway style tiled splashbacks. To the rear of the house is the living room, a generous space with a clever utility cupboard housing the utility appliances. This room is flooded with light from floor to ceiling windows and a patio door which opens out to the garden. Completing the downstairs accommodation is a pristine downstairs WC complete with contemporary white sanitary suite.\n\nUpstairs two beautiful bedrooms await, each offering generous proportions and excellent fitted wardrobe space. The main bedroom also enjoys a fully tiled en suite shower room, and the main bathroom is also fully tiled, with both spaces featuring sleek chrome fittings and high quality, modern ceramic sanitary ware. On the landing, a Stira attic stair provides convenient access to the attic which is partially floored providing ample, easily accessible storage space.\n\nArguably the jewel in the crown of this exceptional home is the garden. A neatly manicured lawn is framed by beautifully planted borders with flowering shrubs and trees creating a lovely backdrop. The spacious sandstone paved patio offers a warm and inviting setting for outdoor dining and those leisurely summer afternoons that effortlessly stretch long into the evening. Enhancing the practicality of the outdoor space, a sturdy double door composite garden shed provides excellent storage and in addition, rear laneway access offers a valuable convenience for transporting larger garden items, bicycles etc.\n\nCastle Farm has been hugely popular with buyers since its launch, thanks to its exceptionally convenient Naas location, spacious layout, and beautifully maintained communal and green areas, and its appeal has only grown over time thanks to the welcoming neighbourhood atmosphere its residents have created! Naas Town is just a short walk away where you?ll find an abundance of bustling cafes, restaurants, shops, and pubs. For lovers of the outdoors, Naas has lovely canal walks and cycle lanes, along with superb countryside to enjoy at both Punchestown and Naas racecourses. Additionally, it is ideally set on the commuter belt, 3 minutes to the M7 exit and only a short drive to Naas/Sallins train station. It has great local amenities including shops, restaurants, Primary and Post Primary schools, tennis, hockey, rugby, golf and GAA clubs. \n\nWe highly recommend early viewing to appreciate all that this lovely home has to offer!"
      },
